{
  "_comment": "HydraPak line sweep, 2026-08-07. The catalog previously carried 6 HydraPak products (Flux 1.5L, PocketFlask, Seeker 3L, SkyFlask Speed IT, SoftFlask Speed, UltraFlask Speed) — this adds the rest of the current line: soft flasks, reservoirs (incl. the full Velocity family), Seeker/Pioneer/Expedition storage, Flux/Stow/Recon/Tempo bottles, filter kits, drink tubes, and the dog bowl. Every weight is HydraPak's published spec for the empty product, quoted verbatim from the product page's spec table. Four items HydraPak's own pages leave the Weight spec blank on are cited from a source republishing the maker's spec sheet (Seeker 6L via Valhalla Tactical — dimensions/material match HydraPak's page exactly; Mountain Stow 350ml via The Trail Runner Store, same check) or an independent review's spec section (Seeker+ 3L via bikepacking.com, whose 28mm Filter Kit figure matches HydraPak's own 47 g exactly). SoftFlask 150/250, FuelFlask, and SpeedCup sell only as 2-packs but the spec weight is per unit (19 g is one 150 ml flask), so rows are single-unit. Tempo Bottle 525ml likewise rows the per-bottle spec from the 3-pack page. Dropped rather than estimated: plain RECON 750ml/1L and WaterGate and Dash Handle (no published weight anywhere citable — the RECON Clip & Carry versions ARE maker-cited and included), Tempo Bottle 400ml (its page's Weight spec is blank), Mountain Stow 350ml would have joined them but for the stockist spec sheet. Out of scope by class: Polar/Breakaway squeeze bottles and MuckGuard (bike), replacement parts and spare caps, cleaning kits/tablets (the co-branded Bottle Bright row already exists), bundles and custom-print variants, POW Stow (colourway of Stow 500ml), FuelKit (a scoop/funnel/tray prep case, not carried gear), Speedfill Pitcher (sideline sports), RECON 500ml (delisted from the storefront). PackFlask+/UltraFlask+/Flux+/Seeker+ integrate filters and take the Water filter gear type per the Grayl/LifeStraw precedent; drink tubes take Hose per CNOC QuickHose.",
